{
  "info": {
    "name": "BFF Dashboard integration tests",
    "description": "MAIR-262: working checks of the BFF Dashboard (the BFF starts, reaches Core, Project and Calendar API, resolves sessions and aggregates the bootstrap payload of the seeded accounts), replayed by newman on docker-compose-integration.yml (./integration_test.sh). The BFF is read-only: it creates nothing, so the collection holds no business journey. The seeded Admin (user 1) and agent (user 2) are impersonated with EdDSA JWTs signed by integration_test.sh with the run's key, like Core signs them (MAIR-680).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// One fresh account per run so the collection is replayable against a persistent database.",
          "if (!pm.environment.get('run_id')) {",
          "    pm.environment.set('run_id', String(Date.now()));",
          "}",
          "if (!pm.environment.get('test_user_email')) {",
          "    pm.environment.set('test_user_email', `newman.${pm.environment.get('run_id')}@mairie360.test`);",
          "}",
          "// MAIR-680: Core alone signs the session JWTs (EdDSA) and the BFF only holds its public key. The",
          "// seeded accounts have no known password and the Postman sandbox cannot sign EdDSA, so their JWTs",
          "// (jwt_admin, jwt_agent, and jwt_forged: Core's kid, another key) are signed by integration_test.sh",
          "// with the run's key and injected by docker-compose-integration.yml. This script only forges",
          "// jwt_hs256: an HS256 token for the Admin signed with a random secret, which must be refused.",
          "const cryptoJs = require('crypto-js');",
          "const b64url = (words) => cryptoJs.enc.Base64.stringify(words).replace(/=+$/, '').replace(/\\+/g, '-').replace(/\\//g, '_');",
          "const hsHeader = b64url(cryptoJs.enc.Utf8.parse(JSON.stringify({ alg: 'HS256', typ: 'JWT' })));",
          "const hsPayload = b64url(cryptoJs.enc.Utf8.parse(JSON.stringify({ sub: String(pm.environment.get('admin_user_id')), role: 'admin', exp: Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) + 3600 })));",
          "pm.environment.set('jwt_hs256', `${hsHeader}.${hsPayload}.${b64url(cryptoJs.HmacSHA256(`${hsHeader}.${hsPayload}`, cryptoJs.lib.WordArray.random(32)))}`);"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
